From: Homelab maintainers <homelab@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: preserve TTL for bridge-originated PPE flows

An IP 5-tuple can describe bridged as well as routed traffic. Honor the
bridge provenance supplied by nf_flowtable instead of decrementing TTL
for all IP entries. Native L2 bridge templates also preserve hop limits.
Routed entries keep their existing TTL decrement bit.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -1444,6 +1444,10 @@
 		return err;
 	}
 
+	/* IPv4/IPv6 5-tuples can originate from a bridge flowtable too. */
+	if (rule->is_bridge || offload_type == PPE_PKT_TYPE_BRIDGE)
+		hwe.ib1 &= ~AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TTL;
+
 	if (flow_rule_match_key(rule, FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_PORTS)) {
 		struct flow_match_ports ports;
 
